The sv_eigen_* files, sv_linalg.{c,h}, and
reference_reloc/c/sv_eigen_pnp.{c,h} are modified Eigen-derived source under
MPL-2.0, not BSD/MIT. LICENSES/MPL-2.0.txt contains the full license;
LICENSES/eigen-notices.txt retains upstream authors and source-file notices.
Calling these modules alone does not label every caller MPL. Distribution
of executables containing them must satisfy MPL source-availability and
notice requirements for the covered files; keep this source with releases.
https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/MPL/2.0/FAQ/

Eigen's Amd.h and SimplicialCholesky_impl.h explicitly record Timothy A.
Davis's permission for the CSparse/LDL adaptations to be distributed as
part of Eigen under MPL-2.0. Those notices are retained. These modules were
ported from those Eigen files, not from GPL/LGPL SuiteSparse modules.

