GPL audit scope and unresolved provenance
----------------------------------------
The inspection covered the complete stella_port tree, source notices,
reference patches, C include/link declarations, and the named upstream
dependencies. No file declaring GPL/LGPL as its own license, bundled
GPL implementation, ORB-SLAM source include, binary library, or symlink
to such code was identified. Documentation references to GPL, native
reference CSparse calls, and MPL's secondary-license wording are not
themselves GPL-covered implementations in the C port.

This is not an unconditional certification that every file is GPL-free.
sv_rng, sv_umap_order and sv_rbtree reproduce libstdc++ behavior. Their
existing BSD-2 declarations have been retained. sv_umap_order documents
measured behavior; sv_rng explicitly records reading GCC headers; sv_rbtree
records reproducing SGI/libstdc++ tree operations. GCC 13 headers carry
GPL-3.0-or-later with the GCC Runtime Library Exception, not LGPL. This
notice pass cannot establish independent authorship from behavior tests
or a source comment alone. Review those helpers' derivation before making
an unrestricted GPL-free distribution claim; adding SPDX does not settle
that question or relicense any copied code.

